1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,610
This is Jun's save file,

2
00:00:02,860 --> 00:00:08,530
day six. The game is called Sunshore,

3
00:00:09,180 --> 00:00:10,930
sunshine, palm trees,

4
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:12,550
a city by the sea.

5
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:14,890
You can drive anywhere,

6
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:16,930
you can go anywhere.

7
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:21,450
But the last place Jun saved is here,

8
00:00:22,420 --> 00:00:24,850
our building, third floor,

9
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:28,570
my door. I'm Ivy,

10
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:31,270
I live next to Jun and I want

11
00:00:31,020 --> 00:00:33,210
to tell you how his game found its

12
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:35,990
way home before I decide whether to press

13
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:36,550
continue.

14
00:00:47,780 --> 00:00:51,510
Night one Jun is 15.

15
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:54,170
His mum works nights at the hospital,

16
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:56,330
so most nights it's just him,

17
00:00:56,460 --> 00:00:58,130
the sofa and the TV.

18
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:00,450
I hear it through the wall.

19
00:01:00,980 --> 00:01:02,330
Usually that's fine.

20
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:05,930
He queued till midnight for the new game.

21
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,330
I heard him come up the stairs two

22
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:08,930
at a time.

23
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:12,310
The first screen is a postcard of the

24
00:01:12,060 --> 00:01:15,050
city, sunshine, palm trees,

25
00:01:15,340 --> 00:01:18,950
the sea, and in the corner where nobody

26
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:21,210
would look, a grey building,

27
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:25,110
our building. Third floor,

28
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:27,430
his window, the light on.

29
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:30,170
He laughed about it the next morning.

30
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:31,890
They must have used a photo,

31
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:34,350
he said. Some designer lives around here.

32
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:37,450
I asked him who was standing in the

33
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:40,390
window. He hadn't noticed anyone.

34
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:52,090
Night two. Everyone online is hunting the ghost

35
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:53,890
car, a white car,

36
00:01:54,040 --> 00:01:56,770
no driver that only shows up at night.

37
00:01:57,240 --> 00:02:00,210
People post blurry clips and argue about where

38
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:04,590
it appears. Jun found it on day one.

39
00:02:05,540 --> 00:02:06,850
Not in the game.

40
00:02:07,940 --> 00:02:10,090
At two in the morning he knocked on

41
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:11,830
my wall, three knocks,

42
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:13,350
our signal for,

43
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:14,390
come and look.

44
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:17,790
From my window I could see it too,

45
00:02:18,140 --> 00:02:19,130
in our car park,

46
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:21,050
under the dead streetlamp,

47
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:24,850
a white car engine running headlights on.

48
00:02:25,900 --> 00:02:30,250
Nobody inside. And from somewhere in the car,

49
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:34,130
very quietly, the music from his save screen.

50
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:37,210
By morning the bay was empty,

51
00:02:37,540 --> 00:02:38,610
no tyre marks,

52
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:41,430
just a dry rectangle on the wet tarmac,

53
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:43,370
the exact shape of a car.

54
00:02:50,020 --> 00:02:54,350
Night three. Jun started writing rules.

55
00:02:54,900 --> 00:02:56,710
That's what you do when a game has

56
00:02:56,460 --> 00:02:58,190
rules nobody tells you.

57
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:02,350
One, never let your character sleep.

58
00:03:03,380 --> 00:03:06,130
Two, if the radio plays a lullaby,

59
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:07,650
save and quit.

60
00:03:08,220 --> 00:03:11,630
Three, never pause on a dark street.

61
00:03:12,380 --> 00:03:16,110
Four, if your character lies down,

62
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:17,530
close your own eyes,

63
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:21,250
two. I asked him why he didn't look

64
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,590
up, so it doesn't close them for you.

65
00:03:25,360 --> 00:03:27,370
And here's the part I keep coming back

66
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:29,230
to. In Sunshore,

67
00:03:29,320 --> 00:03:31,690
the people in the streets had started keeping

68
00:03:31,440 --> 00:03:34,370
our rules, the ones from this building.

69
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:36,650
They pressed the light switch once,

70
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:38,910
they walked, never ran.

71
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:40,670
When the lights went out,

72
00:03:40,860 --> 00:03:41,950
they stood still.

73
00:03:42,820 --> 00:03:44,430
Nobody taught them that.

74
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:47,550
Somebody must have been watching us.

75
00:03:54,140 --> 00:03:58,610
night four. The game gave Jun a choice,

76
00:03:59,120 --> 00:04:01,410
a figure at the door of a little

77
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:03,870
pastel house, two options,

78
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:05,470
let him in,

79
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:07,250
or keep playing.

80
00:04:08,740 --> 00:04:10,410
Then a knock.

81
00:04:11,660 --> 00:04:13,330
Not in the game.

82
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:25,030
On his front door. Same rhythm. Three slow knocks. A pause. Three more. I was on the landing,

83
00:04:25,420 --> 00:04:26,750
I could see his door.

84
00:04:28,020 --> 00:04:30,290
There was nobody on the other side,

85
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:32,070
just the light under it,

86
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:34,990
and in the light the shadow of two

87
00:04:34,740 --> 00:04:38,210
feet. Jun didn't choose,

88
00:04:38,820 --> 00:04:41,150
he stood between the TV and the door

89
00:04:40,900 --> 00:04:43,490
with his thumb over the button until the

90
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:44,290
sun came up.

91
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:48,730
That morning I noticed something about the game.

92
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:52,330
Every night the sun in sunshore set a

93
00:04:52,080 --> 00:04:55,890
little earlier. The palm trees were turning into

94
00:04:55,640 --> 00:04:56,450
streetlamps.

95
00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:07,830
Night five. Jun found the secret ending.

96
00:05:09,180 --> 00:05:10,770
Past the beach,

97
00:05:11,280 --> 00:05:12,210
past the pier,

98
00:05:13,100 --> 00:05:15,030
past the edge of the map where the

99
00:05:14,780 --> 00:05:17,330
painted world just stops.

100
00:05:18,460 --> 00:05:19,610
A grey building,

101
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:22,830
ours. Third floor,

102
00:05:23,340 --> 00:05:24,710
a moth on the window,

103
00:05:25,260 --> 00:05:26,810
old gold wings.

104
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:29,010
He pressed save,

105
00:05:29,440 --> 00:05:32,450
and the real moth landed on his screen.

106
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:34,770
He called me in.

107
00:05:35,200 --> 00:05:36,130
He was smiling,

108
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:38,490
the way you smile when you're too tired

109
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:39,170
to be scared.

110
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:41,450
It's not an ending,

111
00:05:41,660 --> 00:05:45,490
he said. It's a save point for the

112
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:45,870
building.

113
00:05:52,540 --> 00:05:56,990
Day six. His mum came home and couldn't

114
00:05:56,740 --> 00:05:58,790
wake him. Not ill,

115
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:01,290
not hurt, just asleep,

116
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:05,150
deeply asleep, with the controller in his hands.

117
00:06:05,860 --> 00:06:07,450
The doctors say he's fine,

118
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:08,750
that he's dreaming.

119
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:12,350
The console was still on.

120
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:14,350
One save file.

121
00:06:15,060 --> 00:06:17,090
Jun. Day six.

122
00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:20,070
I pressed continue.

123
00:06:20,960 --> 00:06:23,590
The game opened on our hallway,

124
00:06:24,060 --> 00:06:25,870
our light, my door.

125
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:28,590
And in front of my door,

126
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:31,310
a small figure in a dark hoodie with

127
00:06:31,060 --> 00:06:32,370
lime-green cords,

128
00:06:33,080 --> 00:06:37,750
waiting. Then, here in the real world,

129
00:06:38,180 --> 00:06:39,950
a knock on my door.

130
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:42,710
Three slow knocks,

131
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:45,350
a pause, three more.

132
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:48,950
The game is asking me to choose.

133
00:06:49,820 --> 00:06:51,150
Let him in,

134
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:52,530
or keep playing.

135
00:06:53,260 --> 00:06:54,950
I haven't decided.

136
00:06:55,860 --> 00:06:56,950
What would you do?

137
00:06:57,540 --> 00:07:00,130
Some things should stay asleep.
